{"id":"n-20261029-s45arq","category":"finance","display_title":"Human Focus in the AI Era","display_title_he":"מיקוד באדם בעידן הבינה המלאכותית","short_summary":"At ManpowerGroup's The Exchange Israel 2026 conference, corporate leaders discussed balancing artificial intelligence with human talent, adaptable leadership, and organizational agility.","english_level":"C1","words":475,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Male_human_head_louse.jpg/960px-Male_human_head_louse.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Gilles San Martin · CC BY-SA 2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Male_human_head_louse.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3873679","title":"הקרב על הטאלנטים: מי יוביל את עולם העבודה החדש?","published_at":"2026-10-29T09:25:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-29T09:25:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-29T07:08:45.925Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The rapid proliferation of artificial intelligence across corporate environments has sparked a fundamental debate among executive leadership teams. When advanced technological tools become universally accessible to virtually any enterprise, what truly differentiates market leaders from those left behind? This question served as the cornerstone of \"The Exchange Israel 2026,\" an executive conference organized by ManpowerGroup at the Peres Center for Peace and Innovation in Tel Aviv-Jaffa.","Gathering roughly 100 CEOs and senior executives from leading domestic organizations, the event anchored its discussions around the motto: \"Human First. Digital Always.\" The summit forms part of \"The Exchange,\" an international forum established by ManpowerGroup that operates in nations including the United Kingdom, France, Italy, and Spain to connect decision-makers discussing global workforce trajectories.","David Herranz, President of Southern Europe at ManpowerGroup, delivered an international perspective on the macroeconomic forces reshaping global business models. Meanwhile, Dror Litvak, CEO of ManpowerGroup Israel, framed these developments within the local context, outlining five critical priorities for modern management: recruiting and nurturing talent, integrating artificial intelligence, fostering new skill sets, maintaining operational agility, and securing competitive differentiation.","A primary theme of the conference was the imperative for corporate boards to re-examine long-standing operational assumptions. Historically, prior professional experience and past job titles served as the primary benchmarks for hiring and promotion. Today, organizations increasingly prioritize candidates' capacity for continuous learning, cognitive adaptability, and developmental potential. As job functions evolve rapidly, leaders must look beyond filling immediate vacancies to cultivating teams capable of confronting future uncertainties.","Leadership during volatile periods formed another major focus. In a featured discussion moderated by Galit Hami, Boaz Levy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Israel Aerospace Industries, addressed the complexities of strategic decision-making within unpredictable business and security environments. Concurrently, an executive panel titled \"How to Make Change Really Happen,\" also moderated by Hami, explored how companies can translate AI investments into actual business value rather than merely adopting trendy digital tools. Panelists included Guy Kabili, CEO of Afcon Technologies; Amos Bracha, VP of Logistics and Engineering at Ashdod Port; Shlomi Otmazgin, former VP of Development at Yad2 and currently CEO of Velloris.ai; and Shiri Birman-Cohen, Head of the Employee Experience Unit at Strauss Group. They emphasized that intelligent systems must be coupled with workflow design, employee capability development, and human judgment.","Finally, an inspirational session moderated by Tal Berman, titled \"What Do You See That Others Don't?\", examined how hidden talent is identified and cultivated. Featuring basketball coach Pini Gershon and television production figure Tamira Yardeni, the session drew parallels between sports, creative arts, and executive leadership. Speakers noted that coaches, producers, and managers face the shared challenge of discovering unexpressed potential and nurturing a culture of excellence over time.","Ultimately, the conference underscored that technology alone cannot guarantee commercial success; the decisive edge lies in human judgment, leadership, and the strategic deployment of digital capabilities."],"facts":[{"fact":"ManpowerGroup organized 'The Exchange Israel 2026' conference at the Peres Center for Peace and Innovation in Tel Aviv-Jaffa.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Around 100 CEOs and senior executives attended the event under the central theme 'Human First. Digital Always.'","sources":[1]},{"fact":"'The Exchange' is an international meeting platform operating in countries like Italy, Spain, the UK, and France.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"David Herranz, President of Southern Europe at ManpowerGroup, spoke about global business forces, while Dror Litvak, CEO of ManpowerGroup Israel, addressed five core local management challenges including AI integration, talent recruitment, and operational agility.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Galit Hami interviewed Boaz Levy, Chairman of Israel Aerospace Industries, about decision-making during periods of uncertainty.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"An executive panel moderated by Galit Hami featured Guy Kabili (CEO of Afcon Technologies), Amos Bracha (VP Logistics & Engineering at Ashdod Port), Shlomi Otmazgin (former VP Dev at Yad2, currently CEO of Velloris.ai), and Shiri Birman-Cohen (Head of Employee Experience Unit at Strauss Group).","sources":[1]},{"fact":"An inspirational panel moderated by Tal Berman titled 'What Do You See That Others Don't?' featured basketball coach Pini Gershon and TV/production figure Tamira Yardeni discussing talent identification.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"rapid","lemma":"rapid","pos":"adjective","he":"מהיר","name":false},{"text":"proliferation","lemma":"proliferation","pos":"noun","he":"תפוצה נרחבת, התרבות מהירה","name":false},{"text":"artificial intelligence","lemma":"artificial intelligence","pos":"noun","he":"בינה מלאכותית","name":false},{"text":"corporate","lemma":"corporate","pos":"adjective","he":"תאגידי, ארגוני","name":false},{"text":"environments","lemma":"environment","pos":"noun","he":"סביבות עבודה","name":false},{"text":"sparked","lemma":"spark","pos":"verb","he":"עורר, הצית","name":false},{"text":"fundamental","lemma":"fundamental","pos":"adjective","he":"יסודי, מהותי","name":false},{"text":"debate","lemma":"debate","pos":"noun","he":"דיון, ויכוח","name":false},{"text":"executive","lemma":"executive","pos":"adjective","he":"בכיר, ניהולי","name":false},{"text":"leadership","lemma":"leadership","pos":"noun","he":"מנהיגות, הנהלה","name":false},{"text":"teams","lemma":"team","pos":"noun","he":"צוותים","name":false},{"text":"advanced","lemma":"advanced","pos":"adjective","he":"מתקדם","name":false},{"text":"technological","lemma":"technological","pos":"adjective","he":"טכנולוגי","name":false},{"text":"tools","lemma":"tool","pos":"noun","he":"כלים","name":false},{"text":"universally","lemma":"universally","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן אוניברסלי","name":false},{"text":"accessible","lemma":"accessible","pos":"adjective","he":"נגיש","name":false},{"text":"virtually","lemma":"virtually","pos":"adverb","he":"כמעט","name":false},{"text":"enterprise","lemma":"enterprise","pos":"noun","he":"ארגון, חברה","name":false},{"text":"truly","lemma":"truly","pos":"adverb","he":"באמת","name":false},{"text":"differentiates","lemma":"differentiate","pos":"verb","he":"מבדיל, ממציא בידול","name":false},{"text":"marke